# Tab Count Badges — Always Visible

**Every tabbed UI in BazarCRM must show a count badge on ALL tabs, not just the active one.**
Users need to know at a glance how many items are in each section without clicking.

## Pattern Requirements

### 1. API counts (not derived from loaded list rows alone)
Every tabbed page must expose **all tab counts in one response**. Prefer combined **page-data** on mount (May 2026):

```
GET /api/leads/sales/page-data?tab=pipeline  → { leads, counts: { pipeline, follow_up, hold, rejected } }
GET /api/leads/workspace/page-data?…         → { leads, counts: { all, follow_up, hold, routed, rejected, won } }
GET /api/orders/page-data                    → { orders, counts, pagination }
GET /api/crm/page-data                       → { customers, pagination }
GET /api/completed/page-data                 → { orders, counts, pagination }
```

**Pagination:** Tab `counts` reflect all matching rows under current filters but **exclude** `limit`/`offset`. List rows are paginated; reset `offset` to 0 when filters change. Shared UI: `components/ui/list-pagination.tsx`, helpers in `lib/utils/pagination.ts`.

Dedicated counts-only routes remain for lightweight realtime refresh:

```
GET /api/leads/sales-counts   → { counts: { pipeline, follow_up, hold, rejected } }
GET /api/leads/workspace/counts → { counts: { all, hold, routed, rejected, won } }
```

Use lightweight DB queries (`.select("field", { count: "exact", head: true })` or grouped head counts).

### 2. Fetch counts on mount, not lazily
```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — one page-data request returns list + all tab counts
async function fetchPageData() {
  const r = await fetch("/api/leads/sales/page-data?tab=" + activeTab);
  const d = await r.json();
  if (d.counts) setTabCounts(d.counts);
  if (d.leads) setLeads(d.leads);
}

useListPageData({
  cacheKey: `sales:${activeTab}:${filters}`,
  url: `/api/leads/sales/page-data?tab=${activeTab}&…`,
  events: ["bazaar:refresh-counts", "bazaar:leads-changed"],
});

// ❌ BAD — count only known after clicking the tab
useEffect(() => {
  if (activeTab === "rejected") fetchRejectedLeads();
}, [activeTab]);
```

### 3. Badge on every tab — not just the active one
```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — badge always visible, style differs for active vs inactive
{tab.count > 0 && (
  <span
    className="ml-1.5 inline-flex h-4 min-w-[16px] items-center justify-center rounded-full px-1 text-[10px] font-semibold"
    style={{
      background: activeTab === tab.id
        ? "var(--color-badge-bg)"
        : "color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-badge-bg) 70%, transparent)",
      color: "var(--color-badge-text)",
    }}
  >
    {tab.count}
  </span>
)}

// ❌ BAD — count hidden until tab is clicked
{activeTab === tab.id && !isLoading && (
  <span>{tab.count}</span>
)}
```

### 4. Refresh counts after any action
When a lead action changes the data (claim, reject, route, put on hold, resume), always refresh the counts:

```tsx
// After any successful action:
window.dispatchEvent(new Event("bazaar:refresh-counts"));
```

The sidebar, tab counts, and all pages listen to this event and update immediately.

